// Held-out intake set (C04, issue #23).
//
// Written BEFORE the keyword rules were extended for C04, and deliberately not
// consulted while extending them. Its only job is to say whether the rules
// generalise or were fitted to `intake.jsonl`.
//
// That distinction matters more than usual here. The `intake` gate requires 300
// examples per language and the main set holds 20, so the gate reports
// UNEVALUABLE however good the F1 is: twenty examples cannot validate a keyword
// set. This file does not fix that. It is a smaller, independent check that
// catches the most obvious form of the problem, which is a rule matching the
// exact phrasing of the example it was written for.
//
// Synthetic, like every dataset here. No HUTCH traffic and no real customer
// text (I13, I16). `language` is declared by whoever wrote the line, not by a
// detector: the detector is part of what is measured.
